<p>Overall, I think there is a lack of formal tone in the article that could help it seem more like a report and less like a warning about the big scary school, for example;</p>
<p>'Others were as old and wrecked as the main structure.'</p>
<p>Is rather informal phrasing (not to mention it is something of a sentence fragment), perhaps something like;</p>
<p>'Other sections found showed similar wear to initially surveyed sections.'</p>
